# 
# His chapter is a garden with four things in it: an iris bed with a
# heart-shaped box buried in it, a conservatory, a shed he watched her
# from, and a gazebo with a basement under it. Only the gazebo is on
# the way out, but the rest is the chapter.
# 
# The box first. Three nails hold it shut, each of them out, halfway
# or in, and pushing one drags its neighbour round the other way --
# `pushNail` sends the nail after it back a step when this one goes
# deeper, and forward a step when it pops. All three out opens it.
# Walking away puts them back, so it has to be done in one visit.
# Five pushes: the left nail, the left nail, the bottom, the left,
# and the right.
